**Files created:**
- `src/lib/focus-host.ts` — the controller (state machine, history, focus, click delegation)
- `src/components/content/FocusHost.astro` — dialog shell + script mount

**Files edited:**
- `src/layouts/PostLayout.astro` — imports and mounts `FocusHost` right after `FocusTemplates`, same `slug`
- `src/components/content/EvidenceFocus.astro` — added missing `target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"` to "Open in new tab"

**Dialog mount location:** `PostLayout.astro`, not `FocusTemplates.astro`. ARCHITECTURE.md §3 also asks for mounting on the four standalone routes "so a direct arrival still has a working host if the reader opens a child view from there" — I did not do that: those four route files render no `<template>` fragments of their own (that's a template-authoring change, out of this leg's scope), so a host there would have nothing to clone and would be dead weight. `FocusHost` self-guards on thread existence exactly like `FocusTemplates`, so mounting it on those routes later is a one-line addition whenever templates exist there.

